*  alpha_scan_pollution.sno -- witness for row m3-executes-three-times-m4-on-beauty
*  (FINDING-2026-08-22-m3-run-only-is-alpha-cell-scan-pollution.md).
*  Body = corpus/crosscheck/control/expr_eval.sno UNCHANGED (a small recursive-descent
*  expression parser built from deferred patterns/*calls, oracle-verified).  Prepended:
*  100 UNUSED DEFINEd procedures whose only job is to inflate emit.cpp's g_ab_fn_cells
*  table at COMPILE time without changing the program's semantics or its .ref.
*  Mode 3 (BINARY) compiles+runs in ONE process, so these 100 extra compile-time
*  registrations are still in the table when EXPR$-thunk calls (Push/Unary/Binary,
*  routed through rt_dyn_alpha_fn -> bb_ab_slot_for, a linear strncmp scan) start
*  resolving names AT RUNTIME.  Mode 4 (TEXT) compiles in a separate process that
*  exits before the linked binary runs, so the run process's table starts smaller.
*  Measured (RT_OPT=-O0, this .input, callgrind Ir, C1/C3 compile-subtraction for m3):
*    unpadded expr_eval.sno:      m3/m4 run-only ratio ~1.02x (mechanism present, tiny)
*    this file (+100 pad DEFINEs): m3/m4 run-only ratio ~1.29x
*  Same mechanism as beauty (551K rt_dyn_alpha_fn calls, avg scan depth 488.7 vs 104.2,
*  ~96% of beauty's 3.06x m3-vs-m4 run-only gap) at smaller scale; the DEFINE-count
*  landed-subset ceiling (128, lower_snobol4.c) caps how far this specific witness can
*  push the ratio.  See the FINDING for the full beauty-scale measurement and gdb trace.
        DEFINE('unused001(n)')                                     :(unused001_end)
